# CODEOWNERS is an underrated security control. Combined with a ruleset that
# requires review from code owners, it means the security team is *structurally*
# in the path of any change to how the organisation is scanned — nobody can
# quietly relax a gate in a Friday-evening PR.
#
# Replace @your-org/security with your real team slug before this does anything.

# Everything, by default, belongs to the application team.
*                               @your-org/app-team

# Security-critical configuration requires security review.
/.github/workflows/             @your-org/security @your-org/app-team
/.github/codeql/                @your-org/security
/.github/dependabot.yml         @your-org/security
/policy/                        @your-org/security
/scripts/policy_gate.py         @your-org/security
/SECURITY.md                    @your-org/security

# Authentication and crypto code — a second pair of eyes, always.
/app/auth.py                    @your-org/security @your-org/app-team
